1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,423
Chai Corner runs smoothly now.

2
00:00:02,723 --> 00:00:06,075
So Ravi takes a week off,
and nobody is in charge.

3
00:00:06,625 --> 00:00:08,671
On Wednesday, the milk runs out.

4
00:00:08,971 --> 00:00:12,099
On Thursday, the cash box
doesn't match the sales.

5
00:00:12,399 --> 00:00:14,999
By Saturday, sales have dropped by half.

6
00:00:15,649 --> 00:00:17,546
Ravi learns the hard way.

7
00:00:17,546 --> 00:00:19,211
Management never stops.

8
00:00:19,911 --> 00:00:22,165
So, what is management really like?

9
00:00:22,465 --> 00:00:24,126
Let's look at three things.

10
00:00:24,426 --> 00:00:26,676
Its nature: what management is like.

11
00:00:26,976 --> 00:00:28,845
Its scope: how far it reaches.

12
00:00:29,145 --> 00:00:31,331
And its importance: why it matters.

13
00:00:31,981 --> 00:00:34,110
First, the nature of management.

14
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:36,285
These features are true everywhere.

15
00:00:36,635 --> 00:00:37,962
It is goal-oriented.

16
00:00:37,962 --> 00:00:42,616
Every task has a clear aim, like
serving each cup in under three minutes.

17
00:00:42,966 --> 00:00:44,539
It is a group activity.

18
00:00:44,539 --> 00:00:47,721
Ravi works with Asha,
Kabir and Meena, not alone.

19
00:00:48,071 --> 00:00:49,988
It is a continuous process.

20
00:00:49,988 --> 00:00:53,550
Planning, checking and fixing
happen every single day.

21
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,045
It is intangible, which
means you cannot touch it.

22
00:00:57,045 --> 00:01:00,811
But you can see its results:
short lines and happy customers.

23
00:01:01,161 --> 00:01:02,597
And it is universal.

24
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:06,858
A chai stall, a hospital, a
school, even a government needs it.

25
00:01:07,508 --> 00:01:08,852
Next, its scope.

26
00:01:08,852 --> 00:01:11,439
Scope means how far management reaches.

27
00:01:11,739 --> 00:01:14,267
In a business, it covers four main areas.

28
00:01:14,567 --> 00:01:16,523
Production, making the product.

29
00:01:16,523 --> 00:01:17,885
Asha makes the chai.

30
00:01:18,184 --> 00:01:20,309
Marketing, bringing in customers.

31
00:01:20,309 --> 00:01:22,652
Ravi puts up a bright new signboard.

32
00:01:22,952 --> 00:01:24,900
Finance, looking after money.

33
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,561
Kabir counts every rupee.

34
00:01:26,861 --> 00:01:30,476
And human resources, or
HR, looking after people.

35
00:01:30,476 --> 00:01:32,787
Ravi hires and trains the team.

36
00:01:33,087 --> 00:01:38,179
In every one of these areas, a manager
plans, organizes, staffs, directs

37
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:39,268
and controls.

38
00:01:39,918 --> 00:01:42,686
Finally, why does
management matter so much?

39
00:01:43,036 --> 00:01:44,452
It helps meet goals.

40
00:01:44,452 --> 00:01:46,790
Everyone pulls in the same direction.

41
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:48,257
It cuts waste.

42
00:01:48,257 --> 00:01:51,778
Ravi now wastes two litres
of milk a week, not ten.

43
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,706
Less waste means lower cost.

44
00:01:54,056 --> 00:01:56,089
It builds a strong organization.

45
00:01:56,089 --> 00:02:00,184
Next time Ravi takes a break, the
team knows exactly what to do.

46
00:02:00,534 --> 00:02:01,948
And it helps society.

47
00:02:01,948 --> 00:02:06,060
Chai Corner gives three people steady
jobs, and serves good chai to the

48
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:06,997
whole street.

49
00:02:07,647 --> 00:02:08,631
Quick check.

50
00:02:08,631 --> 00:02:12,851
Ravi plans, checks and fixes
things every day, not just once.

51
00:02:12,851 --> 00:02:15,296
Which feature of management is this?

52
00:02:17,196 --> 00:02:18,152
Continuous!

53
00:02:18,152 --> 00:02:20,377
Management goes on every day.

54
00:02:20,377 --> 00:02:21,689
It never stops.

55
00:02:22,289 --> 00:02:23,298
So, remember.

56
00:02:23,598 --> 00:02:28,240
Nature: management is goal-oriented,
a group activity, and continuous.

57
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:32,528
Scope: it covers production,
marketing, finance and HR.

58
00:02:32,878 --> 00:02:36,533
Importance: it meets goals,
cuts waste, and helps society.

59
00:02:37,133 --> 00:02:42,037
Next time, we'll find out if management
is an art, a science, or a profession.
